waypaper for FlickOS
====================

Upstream: https://github.com/anufrievroman/waypaper (GPL-3+). Debian trixie
doesn't have it, so FlickOS packages it natively from an upstream release.

Layout of this folder (installed as is by debian/install, nothing is built):

  usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/waypaper/   upstream's waypaper/ package
  usr/bin/waypaper                          upstream's entry point (the slideshow
                                            runs python3 -m waypaper.waypaperd)
  usr/share/applications/, icons/, man/     upstream's data/ files
  etc/xdg/waypaper/config.ini               FlickOS defaults (not upstream)
  LICENSE, README.md, CHANGELOG.md          upstream's

Changes to upstream:
  - waypaper/config.py: Config.read() reads SYSTEM_CONFIG_FILE
    (/etc/xdg/waypaper/config.ini) before the user's config.ini.
  - waypaper.desktop: without the "#!/usr/bin/env xdg-open" first line
    (lintian).

Updating to upstream release X.Y:

  1. Download https://github.com/anufrievroman/waypaper/archive/refs/tags/X.Y.tar.gz
  2. Replace usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/waypaper/ with its waypaper/, and
     the data/ files (gunzip data/waypaper.1.gz into usr/share/man/man1/).
  3. Make the changes above again.
  4. Compare setup.py's install_requires with debian/control's Depends.
  5. dch -v X.Y+flickos1 -D trixie "New upstream release X.Y."
